00:05:55.520 --> 00:06:00.580
before declaring a weekly hold closed. Two practical tools that could have helped us avoid

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:05.940
that outcome are worth highlighting today. First is implied move from options pricing. This

00:06:05.940 --> 00:06:11.280
technique uses options prices specifically at the money straddles to quantify the percentage move

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:16.240
Wall Street is pricing in ahead of earnings. When implied moves appear cheap relative

00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:22.820
to historical post earnings volatility, it can signal asymmetric opportunity. It gives individual

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:28.300
investors an edge by revealing when the market may be underestimating uncertainty. This allows

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:34.140
better position sizing or volatility based strategies. Intermediate options users on platforms

00:06:34.140 --> 00:06:39.560
like interactive brokers or quest trade can access this directly in the options chain seven to

00:06:39.560 --> 00:06:45.400
10 days before reports. No special subscription is required beyond standard broker tools.

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:52.100
Second is insider transaction monitoring services that surface timely. Form four filings let you

00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:57.380
see when executives buy shares with their own capital. For example, Nike chief executive Elliott Hill

00:06:57.380 --> 00:07:03.640
purchased 23,660 shares. These transactions provide a data point on internal confidence

00:07:03.640 --> 00:07:09.000
though they should never be used in isolation. The edge comes from piggybacking on information asymmetry

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:13.900
while combining the signal with technical confirmation and valuation checks. Canadian investors

00:07:13.900 --> 00:07:20.580
can use free S E C E D G A R searches or paid platforms like unusual whales for alerts.

00:07:21.060 --> 00:07:25.560
Always verify the size timing and whether the buyer has a history of well timed purchases.

