00:09:19.640 --> 00:09:24.660
Now here is something that most retail investors get wrong and it has cost money before the lesson

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:32.640
in. Imagine you allocated $50,000 to a private credit fund in 2024 seeking steady 8% to 10%

00:09:32.640 --> 00:09:37.860
yields with low volatility. Your quarterly statements show consistent returns in a stable net

00:09:37.860 --> 00:09:43.580
asset value but behind the scenes the fund is likely using mark to model valuations instead of

00:09:43.580 --> 00:09:49.060
observable market prices. This means losses from defaults can remain hidden for one to two quarters

00:09:49.060 --> 00:09:53.660
before appearing in reported numbers. Unlike publicly traded bonds that reprise daily

00:09:53.660 --> 00:09:59.060
private loans are valued based on internal models. Current data shows a shadow default rate of

00:09:59.060 --> 00:10:07.400
6.4% while headline figures sit under 2%. One sub segment sits at 9.2%. 40% of borrowers are now

00:10:07.400 --> 00:10:15.580
generating negative free cash flow up from 25% in 2021. Over $350 billion in debt matures in

00:10:15.580 --> 00:10:22.360
2026 and 2027 at rates 2 to 4 percentage points higher than origination professionals always

00:10:22.360 --> 00:10:27.280
demand underlying loan level data vintage year performance breakdowns and manager skin

00:10:27.280 --> 00:10:33.420
in the game metrics before committing capital. They also cap exposure to any single private

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:39.680
credit manager at 5 to 10% of the overall portfolio. You should stress test defaults at 2 to 3 times

00:10:39.680 --> 00:10:44.900
headline figures and maintain strict liquidity buffers. The biggest misconception is believing

00:10:44.900 --> 00:10:51.580
the reported low volatility and steady net asset value reflect economic reality. Instead always

00:10:51.580 --> 00:10:56.980
stress test private credit holdings by assuming default rates 2 to 3 times higher than the headline

00:10:56.980 --> 00:11:02.940
figures. Open your brokerage account whether TFSA, RRSP or non-registered and locate your

00:11:02.940 --> 00:11:07.960
three largest holdings. For each note the percentage of portfolio and whether it would benefit or

